ready: 1
kind: module
id: agents
name: Agents
summary: >-
  Connects agent runtimes to Kernle: answers Claude Code and OpenClaw hooks
  within their deadline, serves the MCP tools to Claude Code and Codex, runs
  the OpenClaw plugin, and installs or removes each runtime's adapter without
  disturbing the owner's own configuration.
runs_in: [sys.cli, sys.claude-plugin, sys.openclaw-plugin]
owns:
  - hook handling
  - the MCP tool contract
  - adapter setup and removal
invariants:
  - A hook never blocks, delays past its deadline, or alters an agent action, except the Kernle-home write guard and a guardrail pause.
  - Installing or removing an adapter never loses a setting or hook the owner wrote.
  - Every tool and hook resolves its stack the same way the Python package does.
rationale: >-
  Adapters are thin: they translate a runtime's events and tool calls into the
  owning modules' operations, so capture, recall, and memory behave the same
  whichever runtime the agent uses.


  Hooks run a native command and hand all work to the daemon over its socket,
  because a hook runs inside the agent's turn and a memory system that stalls
  or breaks the agent's own work costs more than the memory is worth.
